<Base title="Couples Therapy in California | Dongming Zhao, LCSW" description="Emotionally focused couples therapy to help partners understand painful cycles, rebuild trust, and strengthen connection in California." path="/couples-therapy/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="shell reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Couples therapy</p><h1>Move from the same painful cycle toward connection.</h1><p class="lede">For partners who care about each other and want new ways to understand, reach, and respond to one another.</p></div></section>
<section class="section band"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Does this sound familiar?</p><div class="voices reveal"><p class="voice">“Why do we keep having the same fight?”</p><p class="voice">“We love each other, but we don’t feel close anymore.”</p><p class="voice">“I don’t know if I can trust my partner again.”</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell prose reveal"><p class="eyebrow">The pattern between you</p><h2>Understanding what happens beneath the argument.</h2><p class="lede">One of you may push for more talking or reassurance while the other goes quiet or gets defensive. The harder one tries to be heard, the more criticized the other feels, and you both end up alone in it.</p><p>Drawing primarily from Emotionally Focused Therapy, we slow the cycle down, make room for what each of you is protecting, and build enough safety for both partners to feel seen and understood.</p><p>I also draw from IFS, the Gottman Method, and CBT when useful. The goal is not simply to solve today’s argument, but to help build a relationship where both partners feel emotionally safe and genuinely connected.</p></div></section>
</Base>
